| dashyp.hct 1;1 - hyphenation control tbl; breaks at dashes or hyphens
| 1;1 1988-2-17 JES
-hinit 1
| hyphenation mode:
|   0 = no breaks whatsoever (even at dashes)
|   1 = breaks preferably after, possibly before, dashes
|   2 = like 1, but also breaks after internal hyphens
|   3 = Markov algorithm
2
| sequence used for dash (2 chars)
--
| hyphen character
-
| minimum "real" word length to hyphenate at all
4
| minimum length word to leave before break at dash
2
| min to leave before internal hyphen
2
| min to leave before algorithm-break
2
 | spare
 | spare
# | char which, at beginning of wd, excludes it from hy'n (number sign)
| transition-string for beginning-of-word
| !"#$%&'()*+,-./0123456789:;<=>?@ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ[\]^_
 1000000000001010000000011000000000000000000000000000000000000001
2 | no. of algorithm states (>=2, <= 16); req: 0=unsure; 1=end of wd
| !"#$%&'()*+,-./0123456789:;<=>?@ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ[\]^_
 10000001000001             | 0 = uncertain
 10000001000001001111111101 | 1 = at end
| transition-string for excluding pieces all of a class (e.g. lower signs)
| !"#$%&'()*+,-./0123456789:;<=>?@ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ[\]^_
 1000000100001110111111111101
*** | required table terminator
